@startuml SystemArchitecture

'-------------------------------------------------------------------
' StreamPulse Nexus – System Architecture Diagram
' Author: architecture@streampulse.dev
' Last Updated: 2024-06-10
'
' This PlantUML document renders the high-level component diagram
' for the StreamPulse Nexus networking platform.  Components are
' grouped by deployment tier.  Stereotypes map to architectural
' patterns highlighted in project documentation.
'-------------------------------------------------------------------

'========================
'  Global Styling
'========================
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing true
skinparam wrapWidth 200
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam backgroundColor #0f0f10
skinparam component {
    BackgroundColor #1c1c20
    BorderColor #5e5e6a
    FontColor #e6e6e6
}
skinparam package {
    BackgroundColor #131316
    BorderColor #5e5e6a
    FontColor #c3c3c3
}
skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #272730
    BorderColor #5e5e6a
    FontColor #bbbbbb
}

'========================
'  Legend (Patterns)
'========================
legend left
  <b>Pattern Legend</b>
  <&star>  Strategy Pattern
  <&eye>   Observer / Event-Driven
  <&lightning> Command Pattern
  <&layers> Chain of Responsibility
endlegend

'========================
'  TIER: Edge
'========================
package "Edge Tier" {
    [Ingress Gateway] as IG #ADD1
    [Edge Cache CDN] as EC #ADD2
}

'========================
'  TIER: Core Routing
'========================
package "Core Routing Tier" {
    [Media Router] as MR
    [Adaptive Load Balancer\n«Strategy»] as LB <<strategy>> <<(S,#f39c12)>>
    [Event Bus\n«Observer / Event-Driven»] as EB <<observer>> <<(E,#2980b9)>>
}

'========================
'  TIER: Processing
'========================
package "Processing Tier" {
    [Transcoder Pool] as TP
}

'========================
'  TIER: Analytics & Monitoring
'========================
package "Analytics & Monitoring" {
    [Analytics Engine] as AN
    [Alerting Service] as AL
    [Observability Dashboard] as OD
}

'========================
'  TIER: Management & Security
'========================
package "Management & Security" {
    [Configuration Manager] as CM
    [Security Scanner] as SS
    [Backup & Recovery Service\n«Command / CoR»] as BR <<command>> <<(C,#c0392b)>>
}

'-------------------------------------------------------------------
' Component Relationships
'-------------------------------------------------------------------

' Edge → Core
IG  --> EC : HTTP/WebSocket\nUDP Media
EC  --> MR : Routed Media Packets

' Load-balancer Strategy is injected into Media Router
LB  ..> MR : applyStrategy()

' Routing stage publishes events to Event Bus
MR  --> EB : publish(state_change)
EB  --> MR : subscription(callback)  'reverse flow to depict Observer

' Transcoding
MR  --> TP : RTMP/HLS\nRaw Streams
TP  --> MR : Adaptive Bitrate Streams

' Analytics pipeline
EB  --> AN : telemetry\naudience data
AN  --> OD : metrics feed
AL  --> OD : push(alerts)

' Health & Alerting
MR  --> AL : emit(fault)
TP  --> AL : emit(fault)

' Configuration propagation
CM  --> IG : push(config)
CM  --> EC
CM  --> MR
CM  --> TP
CM  --> AN
CM  --> AL

' Security scanning feedback loop
SS  --> MR : vulnerability_report
SS  --> TP
SS  --> EC

' Backup / Recovery command chain
AL  --> BR : trigger(backup)
BR  --> MR : snapshot_state()
BR  --> TP : snapshot_state()
BR  --> EC : snapshot_state()
BR  --> IG : snapshot_state()

'-------------------------------------------------------------------
' Notes
'-------------------------------------------------------------------
note right of LB
  Strategy Pattern
  allows pluggable
  load algorithms
end note

note bottom of EB
  Observer / Event-Driven\narchitecture decouples\nproducers from consumers
end note

note bottom of BR
  Command & Chain-of-Responsibility\ncoordinate cross-cluster\nbackup and disaster recovery
end note

note as N0
  All external communications enforce\nmTLS and adhere to zero-trust policies.
end note
N0 .. BR

@enduml